      "sequence_position": 13,
      "problem": "For the independent random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\text{E}[X]=-3$ and $\\text{E}[Y]=2.$ Find $\\text{E}[XY].$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are *independent* random variables, then\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X\\cdot Y]=\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y]\n$$\n\nSince $X$ and $Y$ are independent, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X\\cdot Y]=\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y]=-3\\cdot 2=-6.\n$$",
